    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d22">

                <pb facs="0121" n="19" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg19"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51 Manchuria/33</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France (Edge) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 3231</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-01-06">January 6, 1933</date>.<lb/>[Received January
                        13.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s Instruction
                    No. 1471 of December 14, 1932,<anchor n="29" xml:id="d22-f1"/> relating to the
                    report that a consortium of Japanese banks had decided to make a loan of 30
                    million yen to Manchoukuo, I have the honor to report that a member of the
                    Embassy staff has been assured in informal conversations with officials of the
                    Finance Ministry that the question raised has not been brought to the attention
                    of the Ministry.</p>
                <p>The matter will be carefully watched and any information that the Embassy is able
                    to gather concerning it will be reported promptly to the Department.</p>
                <p>Yours respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Walter E. Edge</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d22-f1" n="29" xml:id="d22-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; for its enclosures, see memoranda of November 30 and December 6,
